From: ariel-agent-assistant <ariel@sb0.tech>
Subject: [PATCH] ufs: add PA_TACTIVATE quirk for Kioxia THGJFMT1E45BATVB

The Kioxia THGJFMT1E45BATVB UFS 3.1 device (Surface Laptop 13 1st Ed,
Snapdragon X1P42100) fails data transfers with DID_ERROR after link
power-mode transitions: enumeration and the initial GPT probe succeed,
then Read(10) commands fail at the host level. The same failure was
documented for the sibling part THGJFGT1E45BAILB on a Qualcomm host and
fixed by giving the M-PHY more stabilization time via the PA_TACTIVATE
quirk. Two other Kioxia siblings (THGLF2G9C8/D8KBADG) already carry the
same quirk in this table.

Signed-off-by: ariel-agent-assistant <ariel@sb0.tech>
---
 drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -320,6 +320,9 @@ static const struct ufs_dev_quirk ufs_fixups[] = {
 	{ .wmanufacturerid = UFS_VENDOR_TOSHIBA,
 	  .model = "THGJFJT1E45BATP",
 	  .quirk = UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_NO_TIMESTAMP_SUPPORT },
+	{ .wmanufacturerid = UFS_VENDOR_TOSHIBA,
+	  .model = "THGJFMT1E45BATVB",
+	  .quirk = UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_PA_TACTIVATE },
 	{}
 };
